{
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Want to sound like you actually live in Spain? Five words.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_01.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Vale. It means okay. Sure. Deal.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_02.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "You'll say it fifty times a day.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_03.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tío. Tía. Literally: uncle. Aunt.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_04.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "But really? Mate.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_05.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Guay. Cool. Say it like... g-why.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_06.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Venga. Come on.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_07.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Let's go.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_08.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "And somehow... also bye.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_09.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Qué fuerte. No way. That's crazy.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_10.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Use all five in one sentence, and you're basically a local.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_11.mp3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Borderless. The Spanish people actually speak.",
   "url": "file:///home/claude/v4/a/13_12.mp3"
  }
 ],
